---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Brand Identity
description: Visual identity and design standards for Naked Tech — straightforward home technology support for Ivanhoe and Eaglemont.
---

<div class="bg-skin-bone min-h-screen pt-32 pb-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-6xl">

        <!-- Hero / Introduction -->
        <div class="mb-16 md:mb-24">
            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-4 text-electric-peach-ink">Internal Documentation — Brand v1</p>
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-extrabold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-6 tracking-tight">
                Brand Identity
            </h1>
            <p class="text-lg max-w-3xl text-ivanhoe-slate/70 leading-relaxed">
                The Naked Tech brand is rooted in <strong class="text-ivanhoe-slate">transparency, boldness, and local expertise</strong> — built for Ivanhoe homeowners who want technology that works without the sales pitch. This living document defines how those values translate into every design decision.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 01. Brand Positioning -->
        <section class="mb-24 pt-16 border-t border-ivanhoe-slate/10">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-electric-peach-ink">01. Brand Positioning</h2>

            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-12">
                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100 text-center">
                    <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-electric-peach/20 text-electric-peach-ink mx-auto mb-4" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"></path></svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-2">Transparent</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate/70 leading-relaxed">No hardware markups. No hidden call-out fees. What you see is what you pay. Pricing is stripped down to the service and the hardware — shown separately.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100 text-center">
                    <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-electric-peach/20 text-electric-peach-ink mx-auto mb-4" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3.055 11H5a2 2 0 012 2v1a2 2 0 002 2 2 2 0 012 2v2.945M8 3.935V5.5A2.5 2.5 0 0010.5 8h.5a2 2 0 012 2 2 2 0 104 0 2 2 0 012-2h1.064M15 20.488V18a2 2 0 012-2h3.064M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-2">Bold</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate/70 leading-relaxed">We say what we mean. The brand voice is cheeky, confident, and unapologetic — like a technician who shows up on time and actually fixes the problem.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100 text-center">
                    <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-electric-peach/20 text-electric-peach-ink mx-auto mb-4" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17.657 16.657L13.414 20.9a1.998 1.998 0 01-2.827 0l-4.244-4.243a8 8 0 1111.314 0z"></path><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 11a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z"></path></svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-2">Local</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate/70 leading-relaxed">Ivanhoe and Eaglemont are our patch. We know the streets, the housing stock, and the typical NBN pain points. No call-out fees for 3079.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10 border border-gray-100">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-3">Target Audience</h3>
                <p class="text-ivanhoe-slate/70 leading-relaxed">
                    Homeowners in Ivanhoe and Eaglemont (3079) who value their time and want technology that works. They are not looking for the cheapest option — they are looking for clarity, competence, and a technician they feel comfortable welcoming into their home. Secondary: renters, home-office workers, and families managing smart devices they did not set up themselves.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 02. Logo & Mark System -->
        <section class="mb-24 pt-16 border-t border-ivanhoe-slate/10">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-electric-peach-ink">02. Logo &amp; Mark System</h2>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-12">
                <!-- Graphic Mark -->
                <div class="p-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-gray-100">
                    <svg class="h-28 w-auto" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                        <rect x="15" y="10" width="25" height="80" fill="#2D3035"/>
                        <path d="M40 10 L65 90 H90 V10 H65 V90" stroke="#FF8C69" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-linecap="square"/>
                    </svg>
                    <div class="text-center">
                        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ivanhoe-slate/60">Graphic Mark</p>
                        <p class="text-xs mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ivanhoe-slate/50">Rectangle + angular path</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Wordmark -->
                <div class="p-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-gray-100 md:col-span-2 overflow-hidden">
                    <span class="text-6xl md:text-7xl font-extrabold text-ivanhoe-slate tracking-tight whitespace-nowrap">NAKED TECH</span>
                    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ivanhoe-slate/60">Wordmark — Inter Extra Bold, tracking-tight</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Horizontal Lockup -->
                <div class="p-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-gray-100 md:col-span-2 overflow-hidden">
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                        <svg class="h-10 w-auto" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                            <rect x="15" y="10" width="25" height="80" fill="#2D3035"/>
                            <path d="M40 10 L65 90 H90 V10 H65 V90" stroke="#FF8C69" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-linecap="square"/>
                        </svg>
                        <span class="text-xl font-bold tracking-wide text-ivanhoe-slate">NAKED TECH</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ivanhoe-slate/60">Horizontal Lockup (Header Default)</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Stacked Lockup -->
                <div class="p-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4 rounded-2xl bg-ivanhoe-slate border border-white/10">
                    <svg class="h-16 w-auto" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                        <rect x="15" y="10" width="25" height="80" fill="#F7F4EF"/>
                        <path d="M40 10 L65 90 H90 V10 H65 V90" stroke="#FF8C69" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-linecap="square"/>
                    </svg>
                    <span class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-skin-bone">NAKED TECH</span>
                    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-skin-bone/50">Stacked Lockup (Dark Surfaces)</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Clearspace & Minimum Size -->
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100">
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-4">Clearspace</h3>
                    <p class="text-ivanhoe-slate/70 leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        Maintain a minimum clearspace equal to the height of the rectangle in the graphic mark (the dark block) on all sides of the logo. No text, graphics, or interface elements should intrude into this zone.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100">
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-4">Minimum Size</h3>
                    <p class="text-ivanhoe-slate/70 leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        The graphic mark should never appear smaller than <strong>40px</strong> tall. The wordmark alone should never appear smaller than <strong>14px</strong> (text-sm equivalent). The horizontal lockup is preferred for most applications at 32–40px mark height.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Misuse -->
            <div class="mt-8 bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-4">Do Not</h3>
                <ul class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate/70">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink font-bold">✗</span> Stretch, squash, or distort the mark</li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink font-bold">✗</span> Change the mark colors outside the defined palette</li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink font-bold">✗</span> Add drop shadows, gradients, or outlines to the mark</li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink font-bold">✗</span> Rotate the mark or place it on a busy background</li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink font-bold">✗</span> Use the wordmark without the mark as a primary identifier</li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink font-bold">✗</span> Place the mark on a background that reduces contrast (use the dark-surface variant on dark backgrounds)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 03. Color Palette -->
        <section class="mb-24 pt-16 border-t border-ivanhoe-slate/10">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-electric-peach-ink">03. Color Palette</h2>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 mb-8">
                <!-- Skin Bone -->
                <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 bg-white">
                    <div class="h-32" style="background-color: #F7F4EF;"></div>
                    <div class="p-4">
                        <p class="font-bold text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate">Skin Bone</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ivanhoe-slate/50 font-mono">#F7F4EF</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ivanhoe-slate/50 mt-1">Background. Warm off-white. The primary page surface.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Ivanhoe Slate -->
                <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 bg-white">
                    <div class="h-32" style="background-color: #2D3035;"></div>
                    <div class="p-4">
                        <p class="font-bold text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate">Ivanhoe Slate</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ivanhoe-slate/50 font-mono">#2D3035</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ivanhoe-slate/50 mt-1">Text &amp; headings. Dark charcoal with subtle warmth. Hero section backgrounds.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Electric Peach -->
                <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 bg-white">
                    <div class="h-32" style="background-color: #FF8C69;"></div>
                    <div class="p-4">
                        <p class="font-bold text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate">Electric Peach</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ivanhoe-slate/50 font-mono">#FF8C69</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ivanhoe-slate/50 mt-1">Accent. Coral-peach. CTAs, highlights, interactive elements, the path in the logo mark.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Electric Peach Ink -->
                <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 bg-white">
                    <div class="h-32" style="background-color: #B84424;"></div>
                    <div class="p-4">
                        <p class="font-bold text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate">Peach Ink</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ivanhoe-slate/50 font-mono">#B84424</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ivanhoe-slate/50 mt-1">Accessible accent. Terracotta. Accent text and icons on light backgrounds. Meets WCAG AA on skin-bone.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Usage Ratios -->
            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-4">Usage Ratios</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate/70 leading-relaxed">
                    <strong>Skin Bone</strong> should dominate (~70% of visible surface). <strong>Ivanhoe Slate</strong> is the primary text and dark-section background (~20%). <strong>Electric Peach</strong> is used sparingly (~8%) as the accent — if everything is peach, nothing stands out. <strong>Peach Ink</strong> is used only for accent text on light backgrounds (~2%).
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 04. Typography -->
        <section class="mb-24 pt-16 border-t border-ivanhoe-slate/10">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-electric-peach-ink">04. Typography</h2>

            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10 border border-gray-100 space-y-8">
                <div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-3">Font Stack</h3>
                    <p class="font-mono text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate/70 bg-skin-bone rounded-lg p-4 break-all">
                        'Inter', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-3">Weights</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-4"><span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest w-16 text-ivanhoe-slate/50">400</span><span class="font-normal text-ivanhoe-slate">Body text, paragraphs, descriptions</span></div>
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-4"><span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest w-16 text-ivanhoe-slate/50">500</span><span class="font-medium text-ivanhoe-slate">Medium emphasis, sub-labels</span></div>
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-4"><span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest w-16 text-ivanhoe-slate/50">600</span><span class="font-semibold text-ivanhoe-slate">Navigation, section labels, small headings</span></div>
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-4"><span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest w-16 text-ivanhoe-slate/50">700</span><span class="font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate">Card titles, sub-headings, CTAs</span></div>
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-4"><span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest w-16 text-ivanhoe-slate/50">800</span><span class="font-extrabold text-ivanhoe-slate">Hero headings, h1, key numbers</span></div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-3">Scale</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-3">
                        <p class="text-xs text-ivanhoe-slate/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-xs</span> — Fine print, legal footnotes</p>
                        <p class="text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-sm</span> — Body captions, card metadata</p>
                        <p class="text-base text-ivanhoe-slate/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-base</span> — Primary body, form labels</p>
                        <p class="text-lg text-ivanhoe-slate/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-lg</span> — Lead paragraphs, feature descriptions</p>
                        <p class="text-xl text-ivanhoe-slate/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-xl</span> — Subtitles, section intros</p>
                        <p class="text-2xl text-ivanhoe-slate/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-2xl</span> — Card headings</p>
                        <p class="text-3xl text-ivanhoe-slate/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-3xl</span> — Section headings (mobile)</p>
                        <p class="text-4xl text-ivanhoe-slate/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-4xl</span> — Section headings (desktop)</p>
                        <p class="text-5xl text-ivanhoe-slate/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-5xl</span> — Hero headings (mobile)</p>
                        <p class="text-6xl text-ivanhoe-slate/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-6xl</span> — Hero headings (desktop)</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-3">Tracking (Letter Spacing)</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                        <p class="tracking-tight text-ivanhoe-slate/70"><span class="font-mono text-xs">tracking-tight</span> — All headings. Pulls the letterforms closer for a tighter, modern feel.</p>
                        <p class="tracking-wide text-ivanhoe-slate/70"><span class="font-mono text-xs">tracking-wide</span> — Navigation links, brand wordmark.</p>
                        <p class="tracking-widest text-ivanhoe-slate/70"><span class="font-mono text-xs">tracking-widest</span> — Uppercase labels, category tags, section kickers.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 05. Brand Voice -->
        <section class="mb-24 pt-16 border-t border-ivanhoe-slate/10">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-electric-peach-ink">05. Brand Voice</h2>

            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10 border border-gray-100 space-y-8">
                <div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-3">Tone Principles</h3>
                    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate/70">
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink">▪</span> <strong>Cheeky but professional.</strong> The brand uses double-entendre and confidence to stand out from the beige IT crowd, but always lands on competence — never crassness.</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink">▪</span> <strong>Transparent about everything.</strong> Pricing, process, hardware costs. If it can be shown, show it. The "naked" metaphor is not just a gag — it is the operating principle.</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink">▪</span> <strong>Confident, not arrogant.</strong> We know what we are doing and say so directly. We do not overpromise or pretend problems do not exist.</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink">▪</span> <strong>Local, not generic.</strong> References to Ivanhoe, Eaglemont, 3079 — these are not SEO keywords. They are the actual places we serve and the actual people we talk to.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-3">The "Naked" Metaphor — Rules of Engagement</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate/70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                        The brand name is a double-entendre. It works because it is both descriptive (naked = transparent, nothing hidden) and playful. The line is: <strong>playful, never sleazy.</strong>
                    </p>
                    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                        <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-xl p-5 border border-green-100">
                            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-bold text-green-700 mb-2">Do ✓</p>
                            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-green-800">
                                <li>"We turn things on."</li>
                                <li>"Total transparency. Our clothes-off policy."</li>
                                <li>"We handle your hardware with care."</li>
                                <li>"Lock it in."</li>
                                <li>"Secure your slot."</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="bg-red-50 rounded-xl p-5 border border-red-100">
                            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-bold text-red-700 mb-2">Don't ✗</p>
                            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-red-800">
                                <li>Anything that implies sexual availability of staff</li>
                                <li>Jokes about "happy endings" or "extras"</li>
                                <li>Objectifying language about technicians' bodies</li>
                                <li>"We'll make your hardware happy" (too far)</li>
                                <li>Any reference to clients undressing</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 06. Imagery -->
        <section class="mb-24 pt-16 border-t border-ivanhoe-slate/10">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-electric-peach-ink">06. Imagery</h2>

            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100">
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-4">Photo Direction</h3>
                    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate/70">
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink">▪</span> Sun-drenched, warm, natural light — Australian residential interiors</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink">▪</span> Technician-forward: the person is the subject, not the hardware</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink">▪</span> Locations should feel like real Ivanhoe homes — not sterile showrooms</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink">▪</span> Avoid: stock-photo "IT guy in server room" tropes</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100">
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-4">Treatment</h3>
                    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate/70">
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink">▪</span> Slight warmth boost — pull the temperature toward the peach/gold range</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink">▪</span> Natural contrast — avoid heavy HDR or over-sharpening</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink">▪</span> No heavy filters, no monochrome, no desaturation</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-electric-peach-ink">▪</span> Hero images: 16:9 or similar landscape ratio, WebP format, optimized for 2x displays</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 07. Components -->
        <section class="mb-16 pt-16 border-t border-ivanhoe-slate/10">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-electric-peach-ink">07. Components</h2>

            <!-- CTA Button -->
            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100 mb-8">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-4">Primary CTA Button</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate/70 mb-6">The rounded-full electric-peach button is the primary action element. Used in the header, hero sections, and bottom-of-page CTAs.</p>
                <div class="bg-skin-bone rounded-xl p-8 flex justify-center">
                    <span class="inline-flex min-h-14 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-electric-peach px-10 py-4 text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate shadow-xl shadow-electric-peach/30 cursor-default">
                        BOOK A VISIT
                    </span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-xs font-mono text-ivanhoe-slate/40 mt-4 text-center">rounded-full bg-electric-peach shadow-lg shadow-electric-peach/30 hover:scale-105 hover:bg-[#FF7A50]</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Dark Section -->
            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100 mb-8">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate mb-4">Dark Section</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-ivanhoe-slate/70 mb-6">Used for hero headers and high-contrast content blocks. Ivanhoe Slate background with Skin Bone text, Electric Peach accents.</p>
                <div class="bg-ivanhoe-slate rounded-xl p-10 text-center">
                    <h4 class="text-3xl font-bold text-skin-bone mb-2">Total Transparency.</h4>
